<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikhs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikhs</a> are followers of Sikhism, a monotheistic religion founded by Guru Nanak in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in the early 16th century and shaped by nine succeeding Gurus. Persecuted under later Mughal emperors, they were organised as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalsa">Khalsa</a> from 1699 and in the 18th century formed military confederacies, the misls, which carved out states across the Punjab before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> united them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. Most of the world's Sikhs live in the Indian state of Punjab.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikhs.jpg" alt="Sikhs" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: August Theodor Schoefft (1809–1888) [alt. spelt as 'Ágoston'] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Maharaja_Ranjit_Singh_at_the_Darbar_Sahib,_by_August_Schoefft,_ca.1840%27s%E2%80%931855_after_a_sketch_made_by_Schoefft_in_Amritsar_in_1841_(post-varnish_removal).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
